Package: repdist
Title: Structure-Aware Protein Distances, Clustering and Beta Diversity
Version: 0.99.0
Authors@R: person("Yixuan", "Yang", email = "yixuanyang309@icloud.com",
    role = c("aut", "cre"),
    comment = c(ORCID = "0009-0003-5064-6512"))
Description: Structure-aware protein distances from pretrained protein
    embeddings, with clustering and beta diversity built on them. Embeddings
    are computed by models with frozen weights through a pinned Python
    environment provisioned by 'basilisk'; with the default TM-Vec model the
    distance between two proteins is calibrated to a predicted TM-score, and
    it is defined for every amino-acid sequence, including proteins with no
    annotation and no place in a reference tree. Complete-linkage clustering
    groups proteins into structural bins at a chosen minimum within-bin
    similarity, with quality-control plots for picking that threshold and for
    inspecting a bin; bin membership collapses a protein table to bin level
    for downstream testing. For beta diversity, each sample is represented as
    an abundance-weighted distribution over the same embeddings, and samples
    are compared by maximum mean discrepancy under a Gaussian kernel, so two
    samples holding different accessions of similar proteins come out close
    rather than maximally apart. Distances are returned as 'dist' objects for
    direct use with 'vegan' and other distance-based methods.
